WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
- Hello, I mean, congratulations
on all the awards.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.123
- Thank you.

00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:07.200
- Yeah, I mean, like, everybody
hasn't even seen it yet

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.250
and you're already winning awards.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.670
That has to feel pretty fantastic.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.120
- Oh, it's pretty cool, it's pretty cool.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.865
- Yeah, yeah, so, okay.

00:00:13.865 --> 00:00:15.967
So you play a very, even from that scene,

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:17.310
you can kind of tell a
very complex character.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.320
It's kind of this
childhood's been taken away,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.120
but you also have this awakening going on

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.560
as well as an adult.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.080
How hard was that to play?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.000
- I mean, it was a lot of work,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.360
but Sammy's script, there was
so much in between the texts,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.340
so I really just dove into it

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.470
and looked at certain parts of my life.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.730
- I know, did you relate at all?

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.460
- Kind of a little bit, 'cause Joe,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.020
at such a young age, he was a father,

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.320
so it was like this immense
sense of responsibility.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.760
And I grew up an army brat,
so my dad was in the Army

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.180
and he served a few years in the war.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.750
So I remember him sitting
me down when I was 11,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.060
and he just gave me
this inspirational talk

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.180
about being a leader
and honor and integrity

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.053
and like taking care of my two
younger sisters and my mom.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.160
He's my hero, so when he told
me that, I kind of stepped up

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.160
to the plate while he was away
and feeling is maybe similar

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:16.883
but different experience.
- Just having to grow up

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.080
a little quicker in a different way.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.700
I think a lot of us, we go through that

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.310
in different family situations,
so that could be relatable.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.600
But I heard that you also...

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.880
You had to eat, was it fast
food that you ate a lot of

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.380
to gain weight for the role?

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.570
- Yeah, I mean, I didn't have to eat it.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.161
I kind of--

00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:34.080
(laughter)

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.440
- They were like, you should
gain weight for the wrong,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.945
you like ran to all the fast food.

00:01:37.945 --> 00:01:39.840
- Yeah, no, Todd Haynes, our director,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.690
we had conversations about
what Joe would feel like,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.860
not so much look like.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.593
And I was like, I think
this may be my opportunity.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.410
He's a 36-year-old dad,
three kids, provider,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.896
all this stuff.

00:01:53.896 --> 00:01:54.729
Like, he doesn't have
time to go to the gym,

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:57.003
but maybe he has time to eat.

00:01:57.003 --> 00:01:57.840
(laughter)

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.730
- This is my moment to
eat whatever I want.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.780
- Yes, so I ate so much
pizza, fast food, ice cream.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.270
- Nicely done, well, I heard

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.710
this is not your first
experience with fast food.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.080
You actually worked fast
food when you were younger.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.130
Okay, where'd you work?

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:14.190
So my first place was Arby's.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.795
- Classic roast beef.

00:02:15.795 --> 00:02:18.437
- Oh, amazing, they
used to have like the--

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:19.270
- With the Arby sauce.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.850
- Yes, they used to have
like the five for five

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.230
for like 5.95 or something.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.063
- Dude, I know.

00:02:23.063 --> 00:02:23.896
- Yeah, it was amazing.

00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:26.130
So I was there for six months.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.620
After six months, I came home,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.290
I told my dad, dad, I've learned so much

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.480
from just life behind the counter.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.640
And I'm ready to--

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.473
- Move forward.

00:02:36.473 --> 00:02:39.510
- I'm just ready to move
forward and thank you.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.210
I'm gonna just focus in
school and everything.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.043
- Thank you for this opportunity.

00:02:43.043 --> 00:02:44.709
- Thank you, yeah. I'm a
sophomore in high school.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:45.840
Like I'm ready to just...

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:46.740
Thank you, dad.

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:50.160
And he gets a phone call
and he was like, hey,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.160
so your boss told me you got fired, yeah.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.783
- You told him thank
you for the opportunity.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.080
- And he was like, what happened?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.170
And so me and one of my coworkers

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:07.140
after playing ice hockey
with brooms in the back--

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.070
- As you do.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.560
- He threw a curly fry and I ducked

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.170
and the curly fry hit a customer

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.518
in the face and--

00:03:15.518 --> 00:03:16.913
- Wait, you got fired for that?

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:20.793
Not even like a do better next time.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.417
- So I turned in my notice and I left.

00:03:24.417 --> 00:03:26.117
- Oh, you did turn in your notice?

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.910
I love you so much.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.530
So wait, before we go,

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.330
quickly share you have a Wendy's hack.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.700
I love your fast food stories.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.720
- Another fast food story.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.801
- What is your Wendy's hack, yeah.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.290
- So my Wendy's hack because after Arby's,

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.190
my dad's like, we're going to Wendy's.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.613
- Elevated.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.050
- So we go there and yeah,

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.960
so I love working the cash register.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.832
And there's so many
substitutions you can do.

00:03:54.832 --> 00:03:57.510
So I can mix up, I can get a Baconator

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.670
and substitute like the pretzel bread

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.127
or the jalapeno cheddar
bread, or I can do like--

00:04:02.127 --> 00:04:03.240
- You can do that?

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.073
- You can do that.

00:04:04.073 --> 00:04:08.970
It's just like a matter of
how you communicate the order,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:09.930
which I know.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.751
And so they know how to...

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:12.750
There's like no complications at all.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.212
They're just like, oh my gosh, thank you.

00:04:15.212 --> 00:04:17.193
- You're making this so easy.

00:04:17.193 --> 00:04:18.690
It's a dream client.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.643
- Yeah, oh my gosh, you're great.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.920
- Oh my God, I love how
different you are from your role

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.410
that you're playing in this movie.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.820
You are a great actor.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.160
You are so different from
this role, it's amazing.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.090
I love you so much.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.280
Let's do another commercial
break, everybody.

